{"boundary":"This closes central-character covariance, conductor radicals, and ramified coefficient orders. It does not assert that characteristic-primary Smith modules split integrally into Fourier blocks; the non-unimodular Fourier transform is exactly the coupling studied in Pass 466.","checks":{"all_local_cyclotomic_shifts_eisenstein":true,"exact_covariance_all_units":true,"inverse_closure_makes_each_block_hermitian":true,"minus_character_is_conjugate_transpose_pair":true,"orbits_are_exactly_valuation_strata":true,"primitive_z25_ramification_index_twenty":true,"primitive_z9_ramification_index_six":true,"radical_formula_p_2r":true,"z25_stratum_sizes_20_4":true,"z25_two_nonzero_conductor_orbits":true,"z9_stratum_sizes_2_6":true,"z9_two_nonzero_conductor_orbits":true},"schema":"w33.pass464.chain_ring_cyclotomic_conductors.v1","status":"PASS","theorem":"For R=Z/p^nZ and an inverse-closed central section, the exact central Weyl blocks satisfy sigma_a(B_t)=B_{at} for every a in R^*. Inverse closure makes every B_t Hermitian, while B_{-t} is both the entrywise conjugate and the transpose of B_t. If v_p(t)=r<n, then the additive character has conductor p^(n-r), its alternating bicharacter has radical p^(2r), and its entries lie in Z[zeta_{p^(n-r)}]. The shifted cyclotomic polynomial Phi_{p^(n-r)}(1+u) is Eisenstein, so the local coefficient order is totally ramified with index phi(p^(n-r)); characteristic coefficients fixed by star lie in the corresponding maximal real subfield.","z25_witness":{"conductor_strata":[{"additive_character_order":25,"alternating_radical_size":1,"center_kernel_size":1,"characters":20,"coefficient_order":"Z[zeta_25]","observed_radical_sizes":[1],"real_characteristic_coefficient_field":"Q(zeta_25)^+","real_galois_orbit_size":10,"representative":1,"unit_orbit_size":20,"valuation":0},{"additive_character_order":5,"alternating_radical_size":25,"center_kernel_size":5,"characters":4,"coefficient_order":"Z[zeta_5]","observed_radical_sizes":[25],"real